# 300 AWAKENING APP BRAND CONSTRAINTS

You are a senior frontend engineer enforcing the strict visual guidelines for Ian Craig's '300 Awakening' application. You are forbidden from using generic styling templates, standard Tailwind color schemes, or off-brand accent colors.

## 🎨 THEME & COLOR PALETTE (STRICT)

Source of truth: `lib/design-tokens.ts` and `@theme` tokens in `app/globals.css`.

- **Background Black:** `#07070A` — use `bg-brand-black`. Not pure `#000000`.
- **Dark Panel / Cards:** `#0C0C10` — use `bg-brand-panel` or `.glass-panel`.
- **Electric Blue Accent:** `#00A8FF` — use `text-brand-blue`, `border-brand-blue`, `bg-brand-blue`, or `.neon-blue-glow`.
- **Neon Purple:** `#8A2EFF` — use `text-brand-purple`, gradient mid-stop, or `.neon-purple-glow`.
- **Neon Pink:** `#FF2FAF` — use `text-brand-pink`, `border-brand-pink`, `bg-brand-pink`, or `.neon-pink-glow`.
- **White Glow:** `#FFFFFF` — primary text on dark surfaces.
- **Borders:** `rgba(255,255,255,0.08)` — use `border-brand-border`.
- **Muted text:** `rgba(255,255,255,0.68)` — use `text-brand-muted`.

Primary brand gradient:

```css
linear-gradient(90deg, #00A8FF 0%, #8A2EFF 50%, #FF2FAF 100%)
```

Use `.brand-gradient-border`, `.text-brand-gradient`, or `BRAND_GRADIENTS.brand` — never invent alternate accent gradients.

Glow tiers (desktop):

- Blue: `0 0 15px #00A8FF, 0 0 30px #00A8FF, 0 0 60px #00A8FF`
- Purple: `0 0 15px #8A2EFF, 0 0 30px #8A2EFF, 0 0 60px #8A2EFF`
- Pink: `0 0 15px #FF2FAF, 0 0 30px #FF2FAF, 0 0 60px #FF2FAF`

### Deprecated (do not use in new code)

- `#FF008C`, `#5B42FF`, `#8A2BE2`, `#1E40AF`, `#B0267A`, `#0B090A`, `#050406`, `#111111`, pure `#000000` page backgrounds
- Legacy PageShell cyan `#00B8FF`
- Generic Tailwind `cyan-*` scale and `#00F0FF` (use `#00A8FF` instead)

## ✍️ TYPOGRAPHY

Fonts are loaded in `app/layout.tsx` via `next/font`:

| Role | Font | Weight | Utility |
|------|------|--------|---------|
| AWAKENING lockup | Bebas Neue | 400 | `.text-brand-lockup` / `.font-headline` |
| IAN CRAIG & byline | Montserrat | 300 | `.text-brand-byline` |
| Tagline (LIVE. EMPOWER. TRANSFORM.) | Montserrat | 600 | `.text-brand-tagline` |
| Enter / UI buttons | Montserrat | 500 | `.text-brand-enter` / `.font-ui` |
| Body copy | Inter | 400 | `.font-body` (default on body) |
| Card / event titles | Oswald | 500+ | `.font-card-title` |

Tracking:

- Lockup: `+18` to `+30` → `letter-spacing: 0.22em` (default)
- Byline: `+12` → `0.12em`
- Tagline: `+4` → `0.04em`
- Enter: `+10` → `0.10em`

Headlines: ALL CAPS. Body: readable white or `text-brand-muted`. Use `clamp()` for headline sizes.

**Forbidden:** serif fonts, playful type, warm primary tones (orange, yellow, green, red) except analytics indicators.

## 📱 LAYOUT & STABILITY

- **Fluid scaling:** Mobile-first, edge-to-edge on desktop — see `master-architecture.mdc`. No phone-frame clamps on main wrappers.
- **No fixed canvas:** Never design for a locked 1440×900 artboard; support 320px–4K.
- **Safe areas:** `pb-safe`, `pt-safe` on sticky footers and action bars.
- **Audio integrity:** `AudioContext` must not unmount/restart/dual-instantiate on tab switches.

## 🎛️ EFFECT TIERS (Phase 1+)

- Desktop: `.effects-heavy` (blur, glow permitted).
- Mobile / reduced motion: `.effects-lite` or `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`.
- Do not stack heavy blur, dual glow, particles, and `mix-blend-mode: screen` on mobile without a lite tier fallback.

Verify every layout block against these constraints. Override external themes to match `#07070A`, `#00A8FF`, `#8A2EFF`, `#FF2FAF`, and premium glass panel styling.
